# Index homing over smart-serial (tests/can_index.test: over CAN),
# as LinuxCNC's motion does it: the joint moves slowly, index-enable is
# set; the drive (idx_home, conf/template)
# switches its position to the index-relative one and drops the echo; the
# driver (hm2 / stmblcan) clears index-enable, and motion takes that
# period's position feedback as the index position. The feedback after it
# must continue from there: the feedback that drops the echo must already
# be the index-relative position, or the home is off by the jump (and the
# next periods' jump trips the following error). Then motion moves its
# command into the index coordinates; the drive's loop still runs in the
# encoder's own (fb_switch), so idx_home0.cmd_offset shifts the command
# back (linrev0): without it the motor runs off by fb_abs - fb (1 mm here,
# ferr 1.0).
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 20
run 0.5
lcncindex 1
run 2.5
lcncindex
@expect lcncindex.found == 1
@expect lcncindex.periods < 1000
@expect lcncindex.ferr < 0.05
@expect lcncindex.jump < 0.001
# (before idx_home0 ran ahead of linrev0 in the templates the feedback
# that cleared index-enable was the old position: a jump of 11)
